  "conclusions": [
    "The five functional improvements have matching source/report hashes and valid evidence under their all-unlocked, material-rich conditions.",
    "The 35-40x Weird gain removes repeated million-item batch nursery clearing. The ordinary reset already preserves accepted trees within each order and uses paid Weird infection for parallel mature trees.",
    "The underground reset still uses Fertilizer for its nursery. Fertilizer availability is part of reset costs; all-unlocked functional throughput is not its rate.",
    "Long-running Bamboo reuse is useful; the tested 200k reset target completes more slowly and consumes more Rice with full functional flower selection. Extra final Bamboo is reported explicitly.",
    "The functional Sunflower implementation requires 32 drones and a 32x32 map and uses real Pumpkin seed costs for signals. Its small-target exit improvement does not apply to the reset helper, which already checks the goal before every harvest.",
    "Functional pyramid geometry came from the existing pyramid leaderboard. Both reset sources currently use Sunflowers; Jump and explosive-drill assumptions cannot be copied into their startup.",
    "Parallel fixed adjacency construction is correct at 12x12/four drones and saves about 0.57 game seconds once; this is not a material full-route change.",
    "Retaining independent production areas across resource orders remains a structural research direction. Geometry, clear barriers, seed funding and actual critical-path rates must be budgeted first."
